WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.167
This is the Week 9 fingerboard deck. We'll build it the same way you built the skateboard deck in Lesson 2.1, just smaller, and in millimeters.

00:00:10.717 --> 00:00:16.092
Open the document menu, choose Workspace units, and set length to millimeters.

00:00:16.642 --> 00:00:24.316
This part is new. Make a variable called #bolt: the bolt diameter you measured. Ours is 2 mm.

00:00:24.866 --> 00:00:30.613
Make a variable called #clear: the clearance from your Week 5 cube. Ours is 0.3 mm.

00:00:31.163 --> 00:00:36.562
And #hole = #bolt + #clear. That's 2.3 mm.

00:00:37.112 --> 00:00:44.043
Now, just like Lesson 2.1. Start a sketch on the Top plane, and press N to look straight down.

00:00:44.593 --> 00:00:48.064
Press R and draw a center-point rectangle on the origin.

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:53.874
Press C for a circle. Click the midpoint of the left side. Wait for the yellow box.

00:00:54.424 --> 00:01:00.368
Drag to the corner and click. Do the same on the right. The circles make the round nose and tail.

00:01:00.918 --> 00:01:05.864
Press D. Dimension the right edge of the rectangle: 32 mm wide.

00:01:06.414 --> 00:01:10.245
Then click the left tip and the right tip, and type 96.

00:01:10.795 --> 00:01:14.197
Every line is black. The sketch is fully defined.

00:01:14.747 --> 00:01:21.330
Extrude it. In Lesson 2.1 the deck was 10 mm thick. A fingerboard deck is 2.5 mm.

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.585
There's the blank deck. Next, the bolt holes.

00:01:25.135 --> 00:01:27.886
Start a new sketch on the top face of the deck.

00:01:28.436 --> 00:01:36.761
Press R. Move right of the origin until the yellow dotted line appears, and click. That keeps the holes centered.

00:01:37.311 --> 00:01:42.233
Click again to place the corner. Each corner of this rectangle becomes a bolt hole.

00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:51.920
Dimension it with your truck numbers. Ours: 25 from the origin, 8 along, 6 across. Use your own measurements.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:58.217
Use Mirror. Pick the Right plane as the mirror line, then click the four rectangle lines.

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:02.680
Now the second truck has its rectangle too. Finish the sketch.

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:09.708
Open the Hole tool. Choose Simple. For the diameter, type #hole. Termination: Through all.

00:02:10.258 --> 00:02:15.622
Click the four corners of each rectangle. Eight holes, each one bolt + clearance.

00:02:16.172 --> 00:02:21.199
If you re-measure your bolt, change one variable and all eight holes update.

00:02:21.749 --> 00:02:30.701
Last, the fillet. Press Shift+F, pick the top and bottom edges. Lesson 2.1 used 0.125 in. We use 0.5 mm.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:40.155
Here's the deck: 96 × 32 × 2.5 mm, 8 holes. It sits flat, so it prints with no supports.

00:02:40.705 --> 00:02:46.545
To print it, right-click the part and choose Export. Pick 3MF, name it, and export.
